WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.320
It's Tuesday morning at
Wattlevale Logistics.

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:06.740
One delivery on Sophie's run needs
to go to Olivia Parker instead.

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.220
From Oakfield Depot, dispatch can see
which runs are out and which are back.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:13.120
Here's Olivia's morning run.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.160
Her vehicle and route are the same colour,

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.960
and her run sheet shows
her last known position.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:22.020
Before moving the delivery,
dispatch checks the area she covers.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.560
In Route Planning, Metro
West is the delivery area.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.500
The postcode list shows
every suburb it covers.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.020
The order cut-off for the
morning shift is five thirty.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.060
Let's check who's driving.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:37.300
Olivia's rostered on for Tuesday,
the tenth of November.

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:41.540
Clicking her name shows her working
week and the depot she starts from.

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.580
Her run sheet's here too.
Now for the delivery.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:47.080
Order Management opens on the fleet map,

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.280
with every route starting
at the warehouse.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:53.220
Here's Sophie's run. This is
the delivery we're moving.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:56.460
Reassign Order shows every
run that could take it,

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:58.520
and Olivia's has her name on it.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:03.680
Select Olivia. Each plus sign is a spot
in her run where the delivery could go.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:07.100
Pick the one that fits. The dot
marks the selected position.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.580
The review shows the stops either side,

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:11.840
and how the kilometres and minutes change.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.400
The order is still on Sophie's run.

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:17.480
We can compare her run
with an optimised version.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:20.680
For this run, we'll keep
Olivia's other stops in order.

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:24.860
Apply the change. Once it's confirmed,
the delivery moves across.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:26.480
Let's follow it into tracking.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:30.080
In Order Status, search for
the delivery we just moved.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:34.260
Opening it shows the status of it
and the run sheet it now belongs to.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:38.160
There it is, on Olivia's run,
with a stop number and route map.

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:41.600
If the customer rings, dispatch
can tell them straight away.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:46.900
For the bigger picture, Insight reports
on closed-off days. Here's last week.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:51.280
Proof of delivery capture shows the
fleet's result, and how it's worked out.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:55.540
Click into Olivia's Tuesday to
see which deliveries have proof.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.920
Last week or this morning,

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:01.480
dispatch can follow any delivery
from the warehouse to the driver.
